  "MOLE_OFFICE_TELL_THE_OWNER_OF_UNBOOKED_GPU_JOBS": "Whether you are told, beside a GPU booking's holder, when a job with no booking leaves that booking no room on the card. With 1 you are told once for each such job. With 0 only the holder is told, and the Resources page still shows every job with no booking.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_GPU_WATCHER": "The handle of the agent whose watcher reads the host GPU card, overriding the GPU watcher set on the Settings page. That agent and the person may hand in a reading of the card and record a cut-in step.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_HANDLE_BEAT_SECONDS": "How often the waiter says the session answering as a durable agent is still there, in seconds.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_MAIN_WORLD_SUPERVISORS": "How many supervisors may run on the host (not in a sandbox) before the office reminds their starter to use a sandbox: x and a number for so many per secretary, or a plain number for the whole office. It reminds and never refuses.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_MAIN_WORLD_WORKERS": "How many workers may run on the host (not in a sandbox) before the office reminds their starter to use a sandbox: x and a number for so many per secretary, or a plain number for the whole office. It reminds and never refuses.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_HANDLE_LAPSES_AFTER_SECONDS": "How long a session answering as a durable agent may go quiet, in seconds, before its handle stops reading as answering.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_HANDLE_GRACE_SECONDS": "How long a handle stays its session, in seconds, after that session stops saying it is there.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_HANDLE_UNREAD_AFTER_SECONDS": "How long a message handed to the session holding a durable agent's handle may stay unread, in seconds, before the handle stops reading as answering.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_REPLY_REMINDER_MINUTES": "How many minutes a person's message handed to an agent's live session may go without a reply from that agent in the same conversation before Mole Office reminds the agent once.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_MESSAGE_EDIT_WINDOW_SECONDS": "How long after a message is written its writer may still change its words, in seconds.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_ENDED_RUN_LOOK_AFTER_SECONDS": "How many seconds after a run ends the office waits before looking again and reporting its open resources.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_ENDED_RUN_LOOK_EVERY_SECONDS": "How often the office checks which ended runs are due for another look, in seconds.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_ENDED_RUN_SWEEP_EVERY_SECONDS": "How often the office closes gone process rows of all ended runs, in seconds.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_REMIND_ME_LATER_EVERY_SECONDS": "How often the office looks for messages the person put off whose time has come, in seconds.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_LOOK_AT_PRESENCE_AGAIN_EVERY_MS": "How often the server looks again at everybody's presence while a person has a page open, in milliseconds. A test office sets it, so a presence change shows within seconds. The live office leaves it unset.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_RUN_THE_SLEEP_CLOCK_EVERY_MS": "How often the server runs its sleep clock, in milliseconds. A test office sets it to a second, so a sleep whose minute opens is begun within a second. The live office leaves it unset and runs once a minute.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_AGENT": "Which durable agent a session started in this checkout answers as.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_BRIEF_PATH": "The brief file a run started by the office was given, so the run can record how big its brief was.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_FAKE_RUNTIME": "A script that answers every message instead of an agent tool, for the test suite only.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_FAKE_MERGE_TOOL": "A script the message worker starts instead of the office's merge tool, tools/the-merger.mjs, for the test suite only.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_FAKE_INSPECTION_TOOL": "A script the message worker starts instead of the check tool, tools/the-inspector.mjs, for the test suite only.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_HARNESS_REGISTRY": "Where Terminal management reads the newest version of each agent tool, in place of the npm registry and PyPI, for the test suite only.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_RESET_YES_DELETE_MY_DATA": "Set to 1 to let `npm run db:reset` delete a database that holds records.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_REMOTE_PORT": "A second listener on 127.0.0.1 for a private network daemon to pass other machines through to.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_INSTALLATION": "A name for this whole installation of Mole Office, written into the database the first time it is migrated.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_HOME_WORLD": "Which world a run started by the message worker belongs to, when it is working in another one.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_VISIT": "The trip a run started by the message worker is working under, by its id at the office.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_WORLD_STARTED_BY": "The handle of the agent that started this test world, which holds your authority inside it.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_WORLD_SECRETARIES": "The handles holding the secretary card in the office this test world was copied from.",
