  "MOLE_OFFICE_EXPENSIVE_AFTER": "How long a run may be quiet before picking it up again is called expensive.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_LARGE_LAST_TURN_TOKENS": "How many input tokens a run’s last turn must report before picking it up costs more than a fresh brief.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_LOCK_PATHS": "Where the “Running on this machine” list looks for lock files, and the boundary it will register one inside.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_BROWSER_TEST_SLOTS": "How many browser test files may run at once on this machine, as seats the office hands out through POST /api/slots/acquire.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_WHOLE_SUITE_SLOTS": "How many whole test suites may run at once on this machine, as seats the office hands out through POST /api/slots/acquire. Two at once stopped the person's server on 11 September 2026.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_TEST_BATCH_SLOTS": "How many batches of named test files may run at once on this machine, as seats the office hands out through POST /api/slots/acquire to node tools/run-named-tests.mjs.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_TEST_BATCH_LOAD_LIMIT": "The one-minute load average above which the office hands out no new seat for a batch of named test files. A seat already held is kept.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_TEST_BATCH_FREE_GB_LIMIT": "The gigabytes free on the root file system below which the office hands out no new seat for a batch of named test files. A gigabyte is 1,000,000,000 bytes, as df -B1 counts. A seat already held is kept.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_PREVIEW_ROOTS": "Which directories inline preview may serve a file out of.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_AVATAR_MAX_BYTES": "The largest picture, in bytes, that may be uploaded as an avatar.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_MESSAGE_PICTURE_MAX_BYTES": "The largest picture, in bytes, that may be sent in a chat message. Bigger than an avatar on purpose: an avatar is drawn small, and this is a screenshot of a whole screen.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_RETURNED_FILE_MAX_BYTES": "The largest file, in bytes, that may be brought back from outside and stored by the office. A returned file is kept as long as the record that points at it.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_PERSONAL_SPACE_MAX_BYTES": "The most bytes one permanent resident’s personal space may hold. A write that would pass it is refused, naming the size used and the limit; nothing in a space is ever cut or deleted.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_SEED_CORPUS": "The corpus `npm run db:seed` writes, as a JSON file. Unset means the public one in this repository.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_EVENT_RING": "How many recent events the server remembers, so a page that reconnects can be told what it missed.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_ALIVE_WITHIN_MINUTES": "How many minutes of quiet before a durable agent stops reading as online.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_PERSON_ALIVE_WITHIN_SECONDS": "How many seconds since a page said it was still open before the person at it stops reading as online.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_REFUSE_MESSAGE_TO_AGENT_WITH_NO_SESSION_AND_NO_RUN": "Set to 1 to have the message door refuse an agent a recipient nothing is answering as — no session holds its handle, no run of it is going, no connection is open. It defaults to off, and the off is the point: presence is not yet true for an agent started as a subagent, and until M106 (Cluster B) and F9 make it true, refusing on that reading would refuse the live org chart.",
  // The defaults of the next two are owner-decided by a decision, and
