  "MOLE_OFFICE_DEAD_LETTER_AFTER_COUNT": "How many unclaimed dead letters may pile up before the office sends its summary to the named secretary.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_STRAY_GRACE": "How long a server may run, in seconds, before a server with nothing waiting for it is a problem.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_STALE_CODE_GRACE": "How long old code has to stay old, in seconds, before the page draws a red banner about it.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_NO_WATCH": "Set to 1 to start no file watcher. tests/helpers.ts sets it; you never do.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_CHECK_FOR_MISSED_CHANGES": "How often the dev supervisor compares the files on disk with the code the running server loaded, in seconds.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_FAILED_STARTS_BEFORE_SAYING": "How many starts in a row may fail before the dev supervisor writes that where the product can read it.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_A_NEW_SERVER_HAS_TO_ANSWER_WITHIN": "How long the dev supervisor gives a server it has just started to answer, in seconds, not counting its migrations, before it stops that server and starts another. After three such stops in a row it starts none until a file changes. A whole number from 1 to 86400. The dev supervisor counts each server it stops this way in the gate-count spool, with the number of seconds it used. The count begins once the office that reads the gate-count spool runs a version with this row. An office without the row sends each such line to the spool's rejects file, and that line is never counted.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_MIGRATIONS_HAVE_TO_FINISH_WITHIN": "How long the dev supervisor lets a server it has started run its migrations, in seconds, while it answers every request with 503 and the reason. Past this it stops that server and starts none until a file changes. A whole number from 1 to 86400. The dev supervisor counts each server it stops this way in the gate-count spool, with the number of seconds it used. The count begins once the office that reads the gate-count spool runs a version with this row. An office without the row sends each such line to the spool's rejects file, and that line is never counted.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_RESTART_REASON": "Why the dev supervisor started this run of the server, in its own words. It sets it; you never do.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_LISTEN_FD": "The file descriptor of the listening socket the dev supervisor holds for this server. It sets it; you never do.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_STARTED_BY": "What started this server as the Mole Office service. `mole-office start` sets it to `mole-office start`; you never do.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_VITE_CACHE": "Where Vite keeps its pre-bundled dependencies. One cache per checkout.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_PLUGINS": "The folder the plugins are read from, one folder per plugin.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_WORKER_CHECKOUT": "The folder a message worker's runs work in, and where each run writes its rules file. Only a test's scratch office sets it; unset, it is this checkout.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_URL": "Which running browser app the photographing tools open.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_SHOTS": "Where tools/shot-levels.mjs puts the pictures it takes.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_PICTURES": "Turns the picture button on for a photographing run.",
  "HAND_OVER_LAB_SERVER": "The lab server a hand-over copies a backup to. The tool reads it from the environment, then the office's settings file, and refuses when neither names one.",
  "HAND_OVER_LAB_ROOT": "The folder on the lab server a hand-over copies a backup into. The tool reads it from the environment, then the office's settings file, and refuses when neither names one.",
  "HAND_OVER_PROGRAM": "The lab server's program that takes a hand-over's snapshot, by its name or its path. The tool reads it from the environment, then the office's settings file, and refuses when neither names one.",
  "HAND_OVER_LOCK": "The absolute path of the lock file every mover to the lab server holds around each copy. The tool reads it from the environment, then the office's settings file, and refuses when neither names one or the path is not absolute.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_BUS_MOST_ENTRIES": "How many merge entries one whole suite of the merge queue may hold: a whole number from {fewest} to {most}. The suite leaves as soon as it holds this many. It is {shipped} unless set. A changed cap needs the person's press or exact words. The upper bound limits the work of one batch.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_MERGE_WORKERS": "How many test workers the office's merge tool gives one suite run (npm test --maxWorkers): a whole number from {fewest} to {most}.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_MODAL_MONTHLY_CAP_USD": "The most, in US dollars, the merge queue may spend on Modal in one calendar month to run a test file red here once more before an entry bounces, counted from the VM test runner's receipts. It is {shipped} unless set. A changed budget needs the person's press or exact words. Dollar amounts must be non-negative, finite and whole cents.",
  "KIMI_API_KEY": "The key a Kimi CLI run authenticates with. Kimi CLI reads this name and no other.",
  "KIMI_BASE_URL": "The endpoint a Kimi CLI run sends its model requests to, for example https://api.moonshot.ai/v1.",
  "KIMI_MODEL_NAME": "Which model a Kimi CLI run asks for, for example kimi-k2.7-code.",
  "MOONSHOT_API_KEY": "A name for a person's key on Moonshot's global platform, https://api.moonshot.ai. Kimi CLI never reads this name, so the Kimi adapter copies it into KIMI_API_KEY when KIMI_API_KEY is not set.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_PROVIDER_ROUTER": "Whether a dsh run reaches DeepSeek, and an OpenCode run reaches OpenCode Go, through the provider router, a host process that holds the keys and gives each run a token of its own: on, or off. It is off unless set. While it is on, check views and isolated execs get no DeepSeek key and no OpenCode Go key, so the office does not start while a Casting row in force for the inspector uses dsh or OpenCode Go.",
  "MOLE_OFFICE_PROVIDER_ROUTER_RUN_CAP": "The most, in US dollars, one run may spend through the provider router, counted from the provider's own token counts at the price table's prices. With no cap set, the office issues no router token.",
